## Supabase Setup First (Before Writing Any Code)

Supabase gives you a free hosted PostgreSQL database with a connection string you paste directly into Spring Boot. Here is how to set it up:

Go to supabase.com → create a project → go to Settings → Database → copy the "URI" connection string. It looks like this:

```
postgresql://postgres:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@db.xxxx.supabase.co:5432/postgres
```

In each service's `application.yml`:

```yaml
spring:
  datasource:
    url: jdbc:postgresql://db.xxxx.supabase.co:5432/postgres
    username: postgres
    password: your-password
    driver-class-name: org.postgresql.Driver
  jpa:
    hibernate:
      ddl-auto: update
    show-sql: true
```

That is the only change needed. Spring Boot's JPA will automatically create your tables on startup because of `ddl-auto: update`.

